  "en:repo.description": "Description",
  "en:repo.descriptionPlaceholder": "Dispatcher: plans trips",
  "en:repo.draft": "Draft",
  "en:repo.envHint": "If your pipeline deploys each PR to a GitHub environment, Claudio reads the instance address from there. Automatic reviews then only start once the deployment has succeeded, not already on push. Leave empty to use only the URL template.",
  "en:repo.envHintGitlab": " On GitLab a folder such as “review” covers all review apps review/<branch>.",
  "en:repo.envLabel": "GitHub environment of the PR instances",
  "en:repo.envList": "Environments in this repository: X.",
  "en:repo.envMismatch": "“X” is configured, but the PR deployments go to “X”.",
  "en:repo.envSuggestion": "Suggestion: X",
  "en:repo.envSuggestionTail": ", that is where most PR deployments go.",
  "en:repo.expectation": "Expected result",
  "en:repo.expectationPlaceholder": "After saving, a success message appears and the trip is in the list with all its details.",
  "en:repo.extraHosts": "Additional allowed hosts",
  "en:repo.extraHostsHint": "The browser may only visit the instance and these hosts, e.g. a login provider. Separate several with commas; subdomains are included, full URLs are shortened to the host. Applies to reviews, analyses and all tests.",
  "en:repo.extraInstructions": "Additional instructions (optional)",
  "en:repo.extraInstructionsPlaceholder": "e.g. Skip the billing area.",
  "en:repo.flow": "Flow",
  "en:repo.flowHint": "The way you would explain it to a colleague. Claudio creates unique test data itself.",
  "en:repo.flowPlaceholder": "As a dispatcher, create a trip for tomorrow: passenger, time 08:30, from the town hall to the school.",
  "en:repo.forget": "Forget",
  "en:repo.generalIntro": "Notes for the agent and where the pull request instances run.",
  "en:repo.generalTitle": "General",
  "en:repo.githubLoginForCode": "To read the code you need to sign in with GitHub.",
  "en:repo.githubLoginForWebhook": "To set this up you need to sign in with GitHub.",
  "en:repo.githubRejected": "GitHub refused: X",
  "en:repo.glHowCheck": "The status “Claudio” is running while the review runs and successful afterwards: it shows that Claudio has checked the MR, and its text holds the result. If Claudio finds something blocking and “Post the summary as a comment on the MR” is on, it submits the summary as a review that requests changes. A later review without blocking findings withdraws the request.",
  "en:repo.glHowCheckStep1": "In GitLab Premium and Ultimate, requested changes block merging. In GitLab Free they stay a note on the merge request.",
  "en:repo.glHowCheckStep2": "Optional: turn on “Pipelines must succeed” under Settings → Merge requests. While Claudio is reviewing, the merge request then cannot be merged.",
  "en:repo.glHowCheckStep3": "If GitLab refuses the review (older version, too few permissions), the summary appears as a plain comment.",
  "en:repo.glHowPrereqMaintainer": "You have at least the Maintainer role in this project on GitLab.",
  "en:repo.glHowWhat": "Claudio adds an entry in the project on GitLab under Settings → Webhooks. Through it GitLab reports new and updated merge requests, comments, labels, pushes and deployments to",
  "en:repo.glHowWhatAfter": ". Every message carries a secret token that only this project and Claudio know.",
  "en:repo.howAfterA": "a review starts as soon as someone comments",
  "en:repo.howAfterB": "on the PR, adds the label",
  "en:repo.howAfterC": "or (if enabled) pushes new commits. Claudio reacts to the comment with 👀 and posts the summary back as a review.",
  "en:repo.howAfterTitle": "After that",
  "en:repo.howCheck": "The check “Claudio” is yellow while the review runs and green afterwards: it shows that Claudio has checked the PR, and its text holds the result. If Claudio finds something blocking and “Post the summary as a comment on the PR” is on, it submits the summary as a review with “Changes requested”. A later review without blocking findings withdraws that request. To make requested changes block merging:",
  "en:repo.howCheckStep1": "On GitHub: create or edit Settings → Branches → Branch protection rule for X.",
  "en:repo.howCheckStep2": "Tick “Require a pull request before merging” with at least one approval. Open “Changes requested” reviews then block merging.",
  "en:repo.howCheckStep3": "Nobody can request changes on their own PR: if the PR belongs to the person whose access Claudio uses, the review appears as a plain comment.",
  "en:repo.howCheckTitle": "Requested changes instead of a red check:",
  "en:repo.howPrereqAdmin": "You have admin access to the repository on GitHub.",
  "en:repo.howPrereqPublicAfter": ").",
  "en:repo.howPrereqPublicBefore": "Claudio is reachable at a public address (",
  "en:repo.howPrereqTemplate": "A URL template is entered above, so Claudio knows where the instance of each PR runs.",
  "en:repo.howPrereqTitle": "Requirements:",
  "en:repo.howRemove": "deletes the webhook on GitHub. Reviews already started run to completion.",
  "en:repo.howRemoveTitle": "Remove",
  "en:repo.howTo": "How it works",
  "en:repo.howWhat": "Claudio adds an entry in the repository on GitHub under Settings → Webhooks. Through it GitHub reports new and updated pull requests, comments, labels and pushes to",
  "en:repo.howWhatAfter": ". Every message is signed with a secret that only this repository and Claudio know.",
  "en:repo.howWhatTitle": "What “Set up webhook” does:",
  "en:repo.howWho": "Automatic runs use the GitHub access of the person who sets up the webhook. Comments and statuses appear under their name. If someone else sets it up again, that changes.",
  "en:repo.howWhoTitle": "On whose behalf:",
